# Large tiers are fully regenerable (deterministic, seeded) from the scripts
# in minutes — corpus.jsonl (tens/hundreds of MB) and rule_emb.npy (150MB at
# 100K, ~1.5GB at 1M) are too big to commit. The committed source of truth is
# generate_corpus.py + the seed; results/ holds the measured metrics.
corpus/tier_100k/
corpus/tier_1m/

# committed for the small tiers, ignored above that
corpus/**/rule_emb.npy
!corpus/tier_1k/rule_emb.npy
!corpus/tier_10k/rule_emb.npy

__pycache__/
